{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1485537-non-vampire-sheriff","id":1485537,"title":"Non Vampire Sheriff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-01T13:09:09-07:00","id":1485537,"title":"Non Vampire Sheriff","content":"Back in the good old days of the first SARS epidemic, and the War on Terror, some of us were playing a little game with a big title: Vampire; The Masquerade; Bloodlines. The final boss of that game was a mysterious giant referred to as &quot;The Sheriff.&quot; No one seemed to know much about the Sheriff, and one of the few characters who would talk about him suggested the Sheriff might not even be a Vampire. <br /> <br /> Well, now the general consensus is that the Sheriff <b>was</b> a Vampire, just a more obscure one known as the Laibon. But I've been wondering since; what are the odds of a city's Prince recruiting a Non Kindred supernatural as a Sheriff for Kindred society. Something like a Werewolf, or an Ogre Changeling, or maybe a Promethean, if the Prince was one for playing with (divine) fire. <br /> <br /> Has anyone done something like this, in either Requiem or Masquerade? What consequences resulted? What consequences do you <i>think</i> would result?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T13:59:02-07:00","id":1485545,"title":"","content":"I think, they'd make a better hound. I see a good sheriff as more of a 'people-person' role, who can act as an intermediary between the prince and subjects (not necessarily in a friendly manner, but still).<br /> <br /> I mean, you can kinda see the issue with LaCroix. His sheriff is all muscle, which means LaCroix has to do a lot of the talking himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T14:12:05-07:00","id":1485546,"title":"","content":"A game I was in had a pack of Uratha as the personal bodyguards of the ordo prince of the city, the ordo helped the uratha with a plague that decimated their wolf blooded and they agreed to serve as bodyguards and defenders of wyrd nests in exchange, the sheriff was an Ithaeur that voluntered for ordo experimentation and came out with an enhanced physiology that basically had him take damage like a kindred meaning he took bashing from anything that wasn't silver or magic. It worked rather well all things considered, the wolves acted like a professional security detail and were almost never used for the dirty jobs (that was for the player characters), the sheriff himself was actually a really cool character, more of an investigator than a brute (he actually managed to trick our mekhet into revealing a big secret through his skills alone) and definitely a pain in the ass for the whole coterie. Hostile interactions were nowhere the issue we thought it would be since it was an ancillae game and all the PCs had abilities that would allow them to overcome most of the werewolves enforcers (the gangrel character tricked a 4 werewolves squad into killing themselves with animalism). Overall, I would say it is extremely doable for werewolves and I would guess for most other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T21:58:36-07:00","id":1485599,"title":"","content":"Animalism works on Werewolves? But they're not <i>actually</i> wolves.<br /> <br /> Don't they at least get to resist using their primal Urge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T01:09:26-07:00","id":1485610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1485537-non-vampire-sheriff?p=1485599#post1485599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animalism works on Werewolves? But they're not <i>actually</i> wolves.<br /> <br /> Don't they at least get to resist using their primal Urge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which power. Feral Infection definitely works on everything and could be the power referenced. Other Animalism powers generally do not affect anything with higher intellect, <i>but</i> one could always imagine Devotions and Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T01:17:58-07:00","id":1485611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1485537-non-vampire-sheriff?p=1485599#post1485599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animalism works on Werewolves? But they're not <i>actually</i> wolves.<br /> <br /> Don't they at least get to resist using their primal Urge?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Only the first 3 powers of animalism are specific to animals, the rest works on everyone save a few selected beings like revenants, hell I think it actually works on spirits and ghosts too, animalism in requiem is awesome.<br /> <br /> Also yes, the gangrel laid a trap using lord of the land and got the werewolves hit squad to frenzy and tear eachother apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 07-02-2022, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T10:28:47-07:00","id":1485633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1485537-non-vampire-sheriff?p=1485546#post1485546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A game I was in had a pack of Uratha as the personal bodyguards of the ordo prince of the city, the ordo helped the uratha with a plague that decimated their wolf blooded and they agreed to serve as bodyguards and defenders of wyrd nests in exchange, the sheriff was an Ithaeur that voluntered for ordo experimentation and came out with an enhanced physiology that basically had him take damage like a kindred meaning he took bashing from anything that wasn't silver or magic. It worked rather well all things considered, the wolves acted like a professional security detail and were almost never used for the dirty jobs (that was for the player characters), the sheriff himself was actually a really cool character, more of an investigator than a brute (he actually managed to trick our mekhet into revealing a big secret through his skills alone) and definitely a pain in the ass for the whole coterie. Hostile interactions were nowhere the issue we thought it would be since it was an ancillae game and all the PCs had abilities that would allow them to overcome most of the werewolves enforcers (the gangrel character tricked a 4 werewolves squad into killing themselves with animalism). Overall, I would say it is extremely doable for werewolves and I would guess for most other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the killing frenzy saw everyone that wasn't affected by it as a target. So if all werewolves were in frenzy, they would shift into garou and nuke everything nearby except the pack itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T10:43:29-07:00","id":1485634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1485537-non-vampire-sheriff?p=1485633#post1485633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the killing frenzy saw everyone that wasn't affected by it as a target. So if all werewolves were in frenzy, they would shift into garou and nuke everything nearby except the pack itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lord of the land makes you immune to any frenzy, death rage or not, that happens on your territory, you can either point any affected creature towards a target to destroy or just let them attack anything else but you, this includes eachother per feral whispers rule, in this case the gangrel player specifically ordered the pack to kill eachother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 07-02-2022, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}